answer_body:
This outline is used to show that the element is focused (i.e. you can type in the input or press the button with Enter). You can remove it with outline property, though:
`textarea:focus, input:focus{
    outline: none;
}

```

You may want to add some other way for users to know what element has keyboard focus though for usability.

Chrome will also apply highlighting to other elements such as DIV's used as modals. To prevent the highlight on those and all other elements as well, you can do:
`*:focus {
    outline: none;
}

```

⚠️ Accessibility warning

Please notice that removing outline from input is an accessibility bad practice. Users using only a keyboard will not be able to see which element they are focused on. More info at a11yproject

